parts.text:
Fixed everywhere (`c813085`) — and fixed the ivue way: instead of sprinkling `Math.round()` in templates (which the new template-logic rule forbids), the `Pointer` class gains two named plain getters:

```ts
get pageX() {
  return Math.round(this.x.value);
}
get pageY() {
  return Math.round(this.y.value);
}
```

Both the playground route and the docs demo now display `pointer.pageX`/`pointer.pageY`, while the raw `x`/`y` refs stay the public surface for the crosshair pad's math (which *wants* the fractions). Since the docs code tabs show the same canonical files, the example pages teach the fix automatically. Verified: fractional positions (333.7, 444.3) render as `333`/`444` on the docs page and blog embed. 53 commits unpushed.
